  icon: {fileID: 2800000, guid: 42a1298c1cf6c3649ade3d6348fc8ce8, type: 3}
  title: Game Design 1 Readme
  sections:
  - heading: Welcome to the Game Design 1 Unity Template
    text: This is a project template that has some assets already loaded, or unloaded
      depending on your expected needs. It's based on the URP template so it will
      already give you nice foundation to build upon. Below you can find some links
      that can be helpful during your development.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: Local Multiplayer
    text: In case your game will be LOCAL multiplayer it can be daunting to set up
      player prefabs that use the different inputs correctly. To help you with that
      you can find a tutorial video from Unity in the link below.
    linkText: Local Multiplayer Tutorial
    url: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lGxXQzE5Vu8
  - heading: Cinemachine
    text: Cinemachine is already preloaded in this project. IF you want to use it
      you can find tutorials from Unity itself in the link below.
    linkText: Cinemachine Tutorials
    url: https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLX2vGYjWbI0QiMBrmyzbxZeHepAbhVOJa
  - heading: Visual Scripting
    text: The Visual Scripting package is preloaded in this project as well. If you
      feel not comfortable yet coding in C# or want to save time, you can use this
      package to visually code your gameplay using a node-based editor. In the link
      below you find an introduction to Visual Scripting from Unity itself.
    linkText: Introduction to Visual Scripting
    url: https://learn.unity.com/project/introduction-to-visual-scripting
  - heading: ASSETS
    text: Below are some links to assets or asset references that might be handy
      for you. For Assets from the Unity Asset Store, add these to your account.
      Then you can add these in Unity through the Package Manager>My Assets Other
      assets should be imported in your project by manually dragging them in.
    linkText: 
    url: 
  - heading: 'Unity''s First-Person Player Controller '
    text: 
    linkText: First-Person Player Controller
    url: https://assetstore.unity.com/packages/essentials/starter-assets-firstperson-urp-196525
  - heading: 'Unity''s Third-Person Player Controller '
    text: 
    linkText: Third-Person Player Controller
    url: https://assetstore.unity.com/packages/essentials/starter-assets-thirdperson-urp-196526
  - heading: 'Open Assets '
    text: In the link below you can find a compilation of different links to sites
      that collect assets that could be useful in your project. With all of these
      pay attention to the license attached to it. Most will be fine to be used in
      a private educational setting, but some of them could have limitations on using
      them in public.
    linkText: Open Assets
    url: https://github.com/csevier/awesome-open-assets
  loadedLayout: 1
